1
00:00:00,160 --> 00:00:02,190
 The next component that I want to discuss is a

2
00:00:02,190 --> 00:00:06,510
 service. A service is an application component that performs a usually

3
00:00:06,510 --> 00:00:10,000
 long running operation in the background while not interacting with

4
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:13,490
 the user. A typical example of a service, is a service

5
00:00:13,490 --> 00:00:16,260
 for playing music which will run in the background even

6
00:00:16,260 --> 00:00:19,560
 when we are not using the music app directly. Another typical

7
00:00:19,560 --> 00:00:22,070
 example is a download service, such as the one that

8
00:00:22,070 --> 00:00:26,020
 takes care of downloading updates in the background. Once more services,

9
00:00:26,020 --> 00:00:28,370
 they run in the background and they don't interact with

10
00:00:28,370 --> 00:00:31,480
 the user. So they perform some long running function while not

11
00:00:31,480 --> 00:00:35,930
 interacting with the user. Therefore, unlike an activity, services do not

12
00:00:35,930 --> 00:00:38,190
 provide a user interface. Similar

13
00:00:38,190 --> 00:00:40,460
 to activities from the programmatic standpoint,

14
00:00:40,460 --> 00:00:42,680
 the way to create a service is simply to extend

15
00:00:42,680 --> 00:00:45,150
 the service class, and we'll talk more about this. And there's

16
00:00:45,150 --> 00:00:48,150
 just a few things that I want to mention about services,

17
00:00:48,150 --> 00:00:51,330
 just to further clarify what they are. A service is not

18
00:00:51,330 --> 00:00:53,990
 a way to offload some work that should be logically done

19
00:00:53,990 --> 00:00:56,820
 by the application. But the service is a way for the

20
00:00:56,820 --> 00:00:59,180
 app to tell the system about something that it wants to

21
00:00:59,180 --> 00:01:01,770
 continue doing in the background, even when the user leaves the

22
00:01:01,770 --> 00:01:05,069
 application. In addition, a service is also a way for the

23
00:01:05,069 --> 00:01:08,660
 application to expose some of this functionality, for example the music

24
00:01:08,660 --> 00:01:12,940
 playing functionality. By doing so, applications can bind to the service

25
00:01:12,940 --> 00:01:16,850
 and using the service. For example, imagine a turn by turn navigation

26
00:01:16,850 --> 00:01:20,690
 app, such an app will bind to the music player service to be able to

27
00:01:20,690 --> 00:01:23,510
 stop the audio temporarily when making an announcement.

28
00:01:23,510 --> 00:01:23,510
 For example, when a turn is up coming.

